id: 27
hanzi: 高档
pinyin: gāo dàng
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Adjective

meanings_summary:
  en: high-grade; top-quality; upscale; high-end; superior
  es: de alta gama; de primera calidad; exclusivo; selecto; de lujo

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Adjective | Standard | of superior quality, high price, exquisite material, or upscale market grade | de calidad superior, precio elevado, acabados esmerados o gama comercial exclusiva | 高档消费品 (high-end consumer goods)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 商业步行街两侧林立着各类高档时装旗舰店与珠宝专柜，在璀璨的霓虹灯下显得格外繁华。 | Shāngyè bùxíngjiē liǎngcè línlì zhe gèlèi gāodàng shízhuāng qíjiàndiàn yǔ zhūbǎo zhuānguì, zài cuǐcàn de níhóngdēng xià xiǎnde géwài fánhuá. | Both sides of the pedestrian street are lined with high-end fashion flagships and jewelry counters, looking exceptionally bustling under neon lights. | A ambos lados del bulevar peatonal se alinean tiendas de alta costura y joyerías selectas, que lucen vibrantes bajo las luces de neón.
  #2 | 鲁迅宴请文友并不盲目迷信昂贵的高档酒楼，而是更看重菜品的独特风味与席间无拘无束的谈兴。 | Lǔ Xùn yànqǐng wényǒu bìng bù mángmù míxìn ángguì de gāodàng jiǔlóu, ér shì gèng kànzhòng càipǐn de dútè fēngwèi yǔ xíjiān wújū-wúshù de tánxìng. | When entertaining writer friends, Lu Xun never blindly worshipped costly high-end restaurants, valuing unique flavors and uninhibited conversation far more. | Al convidar amigos, Lu Xun no se desvivía por suntuosos mesones de postín, sino que apreciaba el sabor único y la tertulia desenfadada.

